Vendored game-data files
=========================

The following files in this directory are vendored, unmodified, from the
palcalc project:

  db.json        - pal species, passives, active skills, elements, gender probabilities
  breeding.json  - full breeding table + minimum-breeding-steps matrix

Source:  https://github.com/tylercamp/palcalc  (PalCalc.Model/)
Author:  Tyler Camp and palcalc contributors
License: MIT

palcalc is distributed under the MIT License. These data files are included
here under that license as a day-one data contract; pal-calc converts them to
a compact binary pack (pack/paldata.pack) at build time and credits the
original authors. See the palcalc repository for the full license text.

Own-install extraction (Palworld build 24181527)
================================================

  extracted-game-data.json - per-species { elements, partner_skill {name,
                  description}, stats } plus top-level game_settings
                  (Combi_* inheritance arrays + Combi_BossPalRate) and meta.

This file was extracted directly from a legitimately-owned Palworld 1.0 install
(build 24181527) using the tools/pal-extract utility (CUE4Parse + PalworldModding
usmap). It is the AUTHORITATIVE source for:

  - element types (replaces the former vendored elements.json, now removed);
  - partner-skill NAMES (populated for every species);
  - partner-skill DESCRIPTIONS (real in-game text from
    DT_PalFirstActivatedInfoText; populated for every species — replaces the
    former vendored partner-skills.json, now removed);
  - partner-skill ICONS (numeric TextureID keys -> app/public/partner/<id>.png);
  - passive-skill effects, authored descriptions, and lottery/pal-facing flags
    (additive display metadata joined by internal name onto db.json's passives);
  - extended stats (price, craft/slow-walk/walk/run/ride-sprint/transport
    speeds, stamina, max-full-stomach, size).

Note: DT_PalFirstActivatedInfoText descriptions retain the game's own
{PassiveN_EffectValueN}/{ReferenceMsgId_*}/{ActiveSkill*} runtime templates,
which the game substitutes per partner-skill level at display time.

These facts are game data from Palworld (c) Pocketpair, Inc., extracted from a
personal copy and included here for personal, non-commercial use only. All
rights to the underlying data remain with Pocketpair.

Icon assets
===========

The pal icons in app/public/pals/ and the element / passive-rank icons in
app/public/elements/ are sourced, unmodified, from palcalc's bundled art
(PalCalc.UI/Resources/Pals, .../Elements, .../TraitRank). pal-calc renames
each pal icon from palcalc's display-name key to the internal species id
(e.g. "Lamball.png" -> "SheepBall.png") but does not alter the image bytes.

The work-suitability icons in app/public/work/ (12 kinds: Kindling, Watering,
Planting, GenerateElectricity, Handiwork, Gathering, Lumbering, Mining,
MedicineProduction, Cooling, Transporting, Farming) are sourced, unmodified,
from palcalc's bundled art (PalCalc.UI/Resources/). The GenerateElectricity
glyph is palcalc's "ElectricityGeneration.png" renamed to match the
WorkSuitability key; the other eleven keep their palcalc filenames.

Source:  https://github.com/tylercamp/palcalc  (PalCalc.UI/Resources/)
Author:  Tyler Camp and palcalc contributors
License: MIT (for palcalc's redistribution)

These images are ultimately game assets from Palworld (c) Pocketpair, Inc.
They are included here for personal, non-commercial use only. All rights to
the underlying artwork remain with Pocketpair.

Per-species partner skills
==========================

partner-skills.json (formerly the description source; mlg404/palworld-paldex-api
`aura` text, 169/299 coverage) has been REMOVED. Partner-skill names AND
descriptions now both come from the own-install extraction
(extracted-game-data.json, documented above): descriptions are the real in-game
DT_PalFirstActivatedInfoText text at 299/299 coverage, so the derived paldex-api
mapping is no longer needed.

Alpha / UI marker icon
======================

The alpha (field-boss) marker in app/public/ui/alpha.png — the red horned icon
shown on alpha pals — is sourced, unmodified in artwork, from palworld-save-pal's
bundled art (ui/src/lib/assets/img/alpha.webp, itself the game's
T_alpha_icon_normal). It was transcoded from WEBP to PNG (pixels unchanged; a
lossless container change only).

